body:
I tested this PR in my setup. Here are my observations:
- It's probably worth mentioning that `autoApprovers` also need to be configured if you want advertised routes to be approved automatically, since App Connector effectively works as a dynamic subnet router under the hood.
- I couldn't get the full dynamic flow working in my setup. My local Tailscale client doesn't seem to send DNS requests to the app connector node, so no routes are advertised.
- It does start working if I manually send a DoH request to the app connector node for the domain via PeerAPI, for example: `http://100.90.183.244:64526/dns-query?q=ipinfo.io`
- It works as expected if routes are hardcoded in the `appConnectors` section - those routes are advertised immediately. At that point, though, I'm not entirely sure how this differs in practice from regular subnet route advertisement.
- In my testing, adding a new domain to the ACL and running `headscale reload` did not propagate the updated domain list to the app connector node. The app connector node only picked up the updated domain list after restarting the tailscaled service.
- In my tests, `tailscale appc-routes --all` on the app connector node always returned nothing.

It seems like the critical piece here is the DoH flow from clients. I'm happy to help debug/test further, but I still don't understand how Tailscale is expected to route DNS resolution for configured domains through a specific node in the tailnet.

---

This is the ACL config I tested with:

```json
{
    "acls": [
        {
            "action": "accept",
            "dst": [
                "autogroup:internet:*"
            ],
            "src": [
                "group:admin"
            ]
        }
    ],
    "appConnectors": [
        {
            "connectors": [
                "tag:router"
            ],
            "domains": [
                "ipinfo.io"
            ]
        }
    ],
    "autoApprovers": {
        "routes": {
            "0.0.0.0/0": [
                "tag:router"
            ]
        }
    },
    "groups": {
        "group:admin": [
            "admin@",
        ]
    },
    "tagOwners": {
        "tag:router": [
            "router@"
        ]
    }
}
```

`tag:router` is the app connector node, and `admin` is my local machine.

@Matchlighter makes sense, gave it a shot - took a stab at moving it onto `nodeAttrs.app` with the `tailscale.com/app-connectors` cap instead of the custom `appConnectors` block, roughly how Tailscale does it. Had to add valued-cap support to nodeAttrs first (it only did key-only `attr` before), and from there app connectors mostly fall out of the existing machinery.

One thing I liked: it rides the normal `NodeCapMap -> NodesWithChangedCapMap -> SelfUpdate` path now, so I think the `IncludeSelf` workaround can go.

Still need to shake it out, but a couple of things I'm not sure about: the cap ends up shipping on `target` match regardless of `--advertise-connector` (figured the client gates locally anyway?), and I dropped the load-time domain validation in favor of pass-through. Open to feedback on both. The DNS routes + auto-approval part I left alone, still on `autoApprovers`.
